course: dictionary
lesson: 8986
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A sitter can be a babysitter, a pet sitter, a person who poses for a picture, or an easy chance to score in sport. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Pets cannot be left alone for days, so a trusted person or pet sitter looks after them during holidays.» The word pet tells you the sitter looks after animals. So here a sitter is someone who looks after something while the owners are away.
explain: «Mill Lane lose 4–1 and Sam misses a sitter (an easy chance to score).» The brackets give the meaning straight away, and the word match tells you it is a sport. Always check the clues around the word before you choose a meaning.
fact: A sitter can be a babysitter: someone who looks after children while their parents are out.
fact: A pet sitter or house sitter looks after pets or a home while the owners are away.
fact: A sitter can also be a person who sits still to be painted or photographed.
fact: In sport, «misses a sitter» means missed a very easy chance to score.
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning: «Sam missed a very easy chance to score» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
exercise: «Pets cannot be left alone for days, so a trusted person or pet sitter looks after them during holidays.» What is a pet sitter? | A kennel where dogs stay overnight | A vet who checks pets for illness | *Someone who looks after pets while the owners are away | A pet that sits still to have its photo taken
exercise: Mill Lane lose 4–1 and Sam misses a sitter. What does «misses a sitter» mean? | He sat on the bench for the whole game | He was given a yellow card | He fell asleep during the match | *He missed a very easy chance to score
exercise: A sitter can be a babysitter. What does a babysitter do? | *Looks after children while their parents are out | Sits quietly at the back of a classroom | Teaches children to swim at the pool | Paints pictures of children for a living
test: A painter asks Ben to be her sitter for a portrait. What does sitter mean here? | A chair for sitting in | A pet that the painter keeps at home | *A person who sits still to be painted | A babysitter who looks after the painter's children
test: «Kennels, catteries, pet sitters or friends can look after pets during holidays; a sitter lets a pet stay calm in its own home.» Why is a sitter good for a pet? | Because the pet is taken to school each day | Because the pet has to sit still to be painted | *Because the pet stays calm in its own home | Because the pet goes to live in a kennel
exam: Which sentence uses sitter to mean an easy chance to score? | The Rovers hired a sitter to look after their dog | Kennels ask for proof of vaccinations | The sitter sat very still while the artist drew her | *Sam missed a sitter in the last minute of the match
